' --- manual: everything below this line is hand-authored; the script preserves it ---

' The automated pass reads data members and little else, so a repository, a
' service, a handler, a mapper and a registrar all arrive as empty boxes. The
' blocks below fill those boxes and draw the relationships the automated pass
' cannot see.
'
' They use fully-qualified class names rather than a reopened namespace block,
' because this PlantUML version crashes when a namespace that already holds
' classes is declared a second time. Redeclaring a class merges its members
' into the box the automated pass already drew, so a refresh keeps both.
'
' Nine entity families share one shape. folder is the reference instance and
' is stated in full; the other eight are stated once and their repositories
' named the same way, because their contracts are identical apart from the
' domain type they carry.

class ores::synthetic::repository::folder_repository {
    +folder_repository()
    +sql() : string
    +write(ctx, v : folder)
    +write(ctx, v : vector<folder>)
    +write(ctx, v : folder, claim : precondition)
    +write(ctx, v : vector<folder>, claims : vector<precondition>)
    +read_latest(ctx) : vector<folder>
    +read_latest(ctx, id : string) : vector<folder>
    +read_latest(ctx, ids : vector<string>) : vector<folder>
    +read_latest(ctx, offset : uint32_t, limit : uint32_t) : vector<folder>
    +read_all(ctx, id : string) : vector<folder>
    +read_at_version(ctx, id : string, version : uint32_t) : optional<folder>
    +get_total_folder_count(ctx) : uint32_t
    +remove(ctx, id : string)
    +remove(ctx, id : string, version : optional<uint32_t>) : remove_status
    +remove(ctx, ids : vector<string>)
    +get_hierarchy(ctx, root_id : uuid, from_root : bool) : vector<hierarchy_flat_row>
    -replace_claim(ctx, v : folder) : precondition
    -apply_claim(ctx, v : folder, claim : precondition) : folder
}
note right of "ores::synthetic::repository::folder_repository"
The claim is what makes a write safe: replace_claim states
the version the caller read (must_match_version), or that
no row exists (must_not_exist), and the store decides in
the write's own transaction. A row that moved on is a
conflict, never a silent overwrite. remove(id, version)
applies the same rule, and answers removed, conflicting,
missing or unsupported so the caller reports an outcome
instead of catching an exception.
end note
note bottom of "ores::synthetic::repository::folder_repository"
get_hierarchy is the one method folder has and no other
entity does: it walks the self-referencing parent_id tree
and returns flat rows for ores.utility's build_tree.
end note

