note right of "ores::synthetic::service::folder_service"
Every service method takes either the protocol request or a
plain value, so a handler never touches a repository. A
service answers with an outcome -- missing, conflict,
invalid, denied -- inside the response; it throws only when
the store itself fails, and the handler reports that
separately.
end note
note bottom of "ores::synthetic::service::folder_service"
get_hierarchy is the one place the component turns the
repository's flat rows into a tree, via ores.utility's
build_tree.
end note

